	<td bgcolor="#D6CDA3" width="100%" valign="top">
	<font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1"> <b></b></font>
	<p><font face="verdana, arial, helvetica" size="2">Thank you Shei. I was in the discussion with you the other night as Daffan, but kept pretty quiet since I didn't have many facts to go on. I'd like to point out I have never had a problem with SoT prior to this, I don't read RTA (until this happened :P), so I never had a preconceived notion of SoT at all. Even now, there are gaps in info from all parties involved, so much so that I can't really decide what to think. The server community may have rallied behind us on this, and the show of support is certainly makes me feel good, but I still would rather work this out between CoN and SoT. All the support we have, all the SoT bashing that is going on won't change anything. WE have to change it.<br />
<br />
It would be easy to jump on the band wagon and crucify SoT, but I've never personally enjoyed that sort of thing (crucifying nor joining the pack). As far as CoN people sending harrassing tells, I don't approve, but I can't blame them for being mad, even if it is misdirected. For what it's worth, I will ask them to cease, although I'm not the GM or acting GM.<br />
<br />
I don't play as much as I'd like lately, due to college, so I doubt I will be of assistance in game with working out a solution. But I will be active on the CoN forums, doing what I can.<br />
<br />
Once again, thanks for the post. I appreciate it, for what that's worth.<br />
<br />
<br />
Shae</font></p>
	
